  "body": "## What changed\nMove the L-shaped adaptive engagement test to the release heavy lane.\nKeep its fixture, both tool diameters, and every assertion.\nThe file keeps all 17 tests.\n\n## Cause\nThe debug batch reported this measurement taking more than 60 seconds on macOS.\nThe test lacked the ignore attribute that routes heavy measurements to release.\n\n## Tests\nThe external lane-routing pin failed before the fix.\nIt checks the named release lane, unchanged test body, and unchanged test count.\nRestoring the upstream file made the pin fail.\nRestoring the fix made it pass.\nThe exact ignored release test passed with its original assertions in 122.97 seconds.\nThe release dry run includes the motion library heavy lane.\nClippy passed for camcraft-motion with all targets and warnings denied.\nThe quick gate passed against upstream/main with 2 steps and 0 failures in 22.8 minutes.\n\n## Goldens moved\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\nThe macOS debug runtime was not remeasured.\nThe full release gate was not run.\n\n## Overlaps\nPR #1782 touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: Move the slow L-shaped adaptive engagement measurement to the release heavy lane.\nEffort: low\nFixes #1803\n",
